url: "https://musharna.github.io/transposon-genome-ecology/"
abstract: >-
  A watchable, pokeable model of transposable elements as an ecosystem inside a
  genome, in which the unit of individuality is the copy and transposition rate
  is a per-copy heritable trait rather than a player decision. The host's piRNA
  trap is built from captured element fragments, so inserting into it conscripts
  an element into its own suppression. Five questions were pre-registered — each
  with its prediction and falsification condition committed before the code that
  answered it existed — covering per-copy versus family-level rate heritability,
  conscription versus an innate silencer, the fidelity a trap requires, whether
  imperfect trapping yields a band or only a delay, and whether that delay
  diverges or reaches a floor. Documentation, figures and data are licensed
  CC BY 4.0; source code is MIT.
keywords:
  - transposable elements
  - piRNA
  - genome ecology
  - agent-based model
  - pre-registration
  - simulation
